Family Connect @VERSION@ for Linux — the portable archive
=====================================================

Family Connect is a chat for one household, or several, on a server the
family runs itself. This archive holds the same files as the .deb and .rpm
packages, in one folder:

  bin/family-connect       the program
  share/applications/      the desktop entry
  share/dbus-1/services/   what starts the app from the desktop (a click on
                           its icon or on a notification)
  share/icons/             the icon, in 13 sizes, and the top-bar icon;
                           bin/family-connect finds them here, wherever the
                           folder is
  share/metainfo/          the software-centre description
  share/man/man1/          the manual page
  share/doc/family-connect/  CHANGELOG, the licences (copyright) and an
                           AppArmor profile (see below)

Requirements
------------

The libraries of Ubuntu 26.04 or Fedora 44, or later: GTK 4.22, libadwaita
1.9, WebKitGTK 6.0 2.52, GStreamer 1.28 and GLib 2.88 or newer, and
GStreamer's plugins for calls and media. On those systems:

  Ubuntu:  sudo apt install libgtk-4-1 libadwaita-1-0 libwebkitgtk-6.0-4 \
               libgstreamer1.0-0 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base \
               gstreamer1.0-plugins-good gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad \
               gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly gstreamer1.0-libav \
               gstreamer1.0-nice gstreamer1.0-pipewire gstreamer1.0-gtk4 \
               glib-networking libsecret-1-0 libsqlite3-0
  Fedora:  sudo dnf install gtk4 libadwaita webkitgtk6.0 gstreamer1 \
               gstreamer1-plugins-base gstreamer1-plugins-good \
               gstreamer1-plugins-bad-free gstreamer1-plugin-libav \
               gstreamer1-plugin-openh264 gstreamer1-plugin-gtk4 \
               libnice-gstreamer1 pipewire-gstreamer glib-networking \
               libsecret sqlite-libs

It keeps its sign-in in the Secret Service (GNOME Keyring) and reaches the
camera and notifications through the desktop portals
(xdg-desktop-portal-gnome), which Ubuntu Desktop and Fedora Workstation
install.

Where the .deb or .rpm fits, prefer it: the package manager brings all of
this, and on Ubuntu the .deb also installs the AppArmor profile.

Run it
------

  tar -xzf family-connect-@VERSION@-linux-*.tar.gz
  family-connect-@VERSION@/bin/family-connect

To install it for yourself, with Family Connect in the app grid:

  cp -r family-connect-@VERSION@/bin family-connect-@VERSION@/share ~/.local/
  sed -i "s|^Exec=/usr/bin/|Exec=$HOME/.local/bin/|" \
      ~/.local/share/dbus-1/services/me.nettrash.FamilyConnect.service
  update-desktop-database ~/.local/share/applications

and make sure ~/.local/bin is on your PATH. To remove it, delete what was
copied: ~/.local/bin/family-connect, ~/.local/share/doc/family-connect,
~/.local/share/man/man1/family-connect.1.gz, and the files named
me.nettrash.FamilyConnect* under ~/.local/share.

Ubuntu 24.04 and later
----------------------

Family Connect draws parts of its window with WebKit, whose sandbox needs a
user namespace, and Ubuntu lets a program create one only when an AppArmor
profile allows it. The .deb installs that profile for
/usr/bin/family-connect. For this archive, copy
share/doc/family-connect/apparmor-profile to /etc/apparmor.d/family-connect,
change /usr/bin/family-connect in it to the full path of bin/family-connect,
and load it:

  sudo apparmor_parser -r /etc/apparmor.d/family-connect

https://nettrash.me/linux/familyconnect/support.html
